The program first establishes the array that will be used.
It then loops through each element in the array to find duplicates.
It then will check to see if the current element has already been reported to prevent duplicate reporting of duplicates.
After that, it will check the elements that come before the current element to see if there are duplicates.
It will do the same for the elements that come after it.
If a duplicate is found, it will be reported and stop checking for duplicates.
It then prints out all the duplicates found once.
*/
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        //Don't let the size of this scare you! no matter how big an array is, it all works the same!
        int[] myArray = {10,3,295,38,20,3,4,267,2445,10,5566,87,93,17,10,2,87,267,3176,3,82};
        //you cannot use the array util. Do this one by hand :(

        for (int i = 0; i < myArray.length; i++) { // Loops through each element

            boolean alreadyReported = false; // Checks if the element has been reported before

            for (int k = 0; k < i; k++) { // Checks all previous elements
                if (myArray[i] == myArray[k]) { // Compares current element with previous elements
                    alreadyReported = true; // Already printed this number
                    break; // Stop checking previous elements
                }
            }

            if (!alreadyReported) { // Only continue if this number hasn't been reported yet

                boolean isDuplicate = false;

                for (int j = i + 1; j < myArray.length; j++) { // Check all elements after the current one
                    if (myArray[i] == myArray[j]) { // Compares element with next elements
                        isDuplicate = true; // Found a duplicate
                        break; // Stop checking next elements
                    }
                }
                
                if (isDuplicate) { // Print the duplicate number
                    System.out.println("Duplicate Number: " + myArray[i]);
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
